  <field id="fieldset_0-63_11" has_partial_fieldset="False" is_linked_to_partial_fieldset="False" is_access_restriction_possible="False" is_variable_length="False" is_constant_value="False" is_partial_field="False" is_conditional_field_name="False">
    <field_name>VBA</field_name>
    <field_shortdesc>Vector Base Address</field_shortdesc>
    <field_msb>63</field_msb>
    <field_lsb>11</field_lsb>
    <rel_range>63:11</rel_range>
    <field_description order="before"><para>Vector Base Address. Base address of the exception vectors for exceptions taken to EL3.</para>
<note><para>If the implementation supports <xref linkend="#FEAT_LVA3">FEAT_LVA3</xref>, then:</para><list type="unordered"><listitem><content>If tagged addresses are not being used, bits [63:56] of VBAR_EL3 must be 0 or else the use of the vector address will result in a recursive exception.</content></listitem></list><para>Otherwise:</para><para>If the implementation supports <xref linkend="#FEAT_LVA">FEAT_LVA</xref>, then:</para><list type="unordered"><listitem><content>If tagged addresses are being used, bits [55:52] of VBAR_EL3 must be 0 or else the use of the vector address will result in a recursive exception.</content></listitem><listitem><content>If tagged addresses are not being used, bits [63:52] of VBAR_EL3 must be 0 or else the use of the vector address will result in a recursive exception.</content></listitem></list><para>If the implementation does not support <xref linkend="#FEAT_LVA">FEAT_LVA</xref>, then:</para><list type="unordered"><listitem><content>If tagged addresses are being used, bits [55:48] of VBAR_EL3 must be 0 or else the use of the vector address will result in a recursive exception.</content></listitem><listitem><content>If tagged addresses are not being used, bits [63:48] of VBAR_EL3 must be 0 or else the use of the vector address will result in a recursive exception.</content></listitem></list></note></field_description>
    <field_resets>
      <field_reset reset_type="Warm">
        <field_reset_standard_text>AU</field_reset_standard_text>
      </field_reset>
    </field_resets>
  </field>
